{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1c90b86d4e8b96db524ccf6dcd9f644b80fcb71a713068a8aa99dca13fd6d17b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The toolkit prescribes a traceable artifact chain — PRD (what), SPEC (how), ADR (why), TASK (steps) — flowing through code, review, deploy, and closed by a sprint retrospective."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1c90b86d4e8b96db524ccf6dcd9f644b80fcb71a713068a8aa99dca13fd6d17b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","id":"pg_570ab76b21875773bc04fb196b13fea1","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/polymathwizard-bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit-01-methodology-overvi-fb196b13fea1.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_422bf43bb6c7517498436983e31c26c6"],"title":"PolymathWizard/BHIL-AI-First-Development-Toolkit/01-methodology-overview.md @ 161f8e5311bd","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","id":"pg_6d21dd4d11c25020a2f40c3383baa04d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/polymathwizard-bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit-architecture-md-161f8-0c3383baa04d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_896f2a5921b552c1bd89b7f08727469c"],"title":"PolymathWizard/BHIL-AI-First-Development-Toolkit/architecture.md @ 161f8e5311bd","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1c90b86d4e8b96db524ccf6dcd9f644b80fcb71a713068a8aa99dca13fd6d17b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The toolkit prescribes a traceable artifact chain — PRD (what), SPEC (how), ADR (why), TASK (steps) — flowing through code, review, deploy, and closed by a sprint retrospective."},{"claim_ids":["clm_27451c3268805d2a8496acaa1f7f12edf909de6bba7c96be5d90dfd8a709318f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Beyond standard ADRs, the toolkit defines three AI-native ADR categories — model selection, prompt strategy, and agent orchestration — each with its own template."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3c7ce68dbbf6eee3d825392e647d9a80732755843ada1872d762ea421e26cc1d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Traceability links are asymmetric: children reference parents (e.g., SPECs reference parent PRD-NNN; TASKs reference spec and ADRs), while PRDs reference nothing upstream."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5f36c5ea8b6ce0a874be89d00de2a3c9c45d6479e32ba7b4c75b8ea395571645"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every artifact carries a traceability ID in YAML frontmatter with defined formats such as PRD-NNN, SPEC-NNN, ADR-NNN, TASK-NNN, S-NN, and PV-NNN."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7fc09b5b0759d72c0499d8cf22b7d2352a6042e18241b3089ba761325f1831d3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository ships copy-and-fill templates including PRD, SPEC, TASK, sprint plan, and four ADR variants: core MADR-style, model-selection, prompt-strategy, and agent-orchestration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a62a0b97bad6c36191699dc2cdf0c0e2576a5162cbc4d85f869a3020fae4cff5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The methodology assigns RuVector the role of maintaining persistent memory across sessions so agent context does not start cold; RuFlo optionally orchestrates agents across the artifact chain."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c4b1ff73576888c48feeb92f86ad5c0a074f1abb8d16c1b66019a397cc770dcf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The toolkit is released under the MIT License, with copyright attributed to BarryHurd.com."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1c90b86d4e8b96db524ccf6dcd9f644b80fcb71a713068a8aa99dca13fd6d17b","clm_27451c3268805d2a8496acaa1f7f12edf909de6bba7c96be5d90dfd8a709318f","clm_3c7ce68dbbf6eee3d825392e647d9a80732755843ada1872d762ea421e26cc1d","clm_5f36c5ea8b6ce0a874be89d00de2a3c9c45d6479e32ba7b4c75b8ea395571645","clm_7fc09b5b0759d72c0499d8cf22b7d2352a6042e18241b3089ba761325f1831d3","clm_a62a0b97bad6c36191699dc2cdf0c0e2576a5162cbc4d85f869a3020fae4cff5","clm_c4b1ff73576888c48feeb92f86ad5c0a074f1abb8d16c1b66019a397cc770dcf"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","created_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771","id":"pg_bdf4c042e7bb517c8d90250efd5b0dc6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/polymathwizard-bhil-ai-first-development-toolkit-readme-md-161f8e5311b-250efd5b0dc6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_842d991c73375108b27a474a2492c958"],"title":"PolymathWizard/BHIL-AI-First-Development-Toolkit/README.md @ 161f8e5311bd","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:16:31Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4fa9bbd9608c40b2a0df9c3d08c54771"}
